WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.400
The park and preserve spans over 4 million acres and is larger than the size of Connecticut and Rhode Island combined.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.560
Lake Clark was created by the landmark 1980 Alaska National Interest Lands Conservation Act.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:33.380
This act protects Alaska's wildlands and maintains traditional hunting, fishing, and foraging activities that people have engaged in since before the designation of many Alaska National Parks.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:40.900
In this realm without roads, local people are inspired and sustained by the land and water.
